---Database instance clone context.
---@class gcp.sqladmin_v1.CloneContext
---@field preferredSecondaryZone? string Optional. Copy clone and point-in-time recovery clone of a regional instance in the specified zones. If not specified, clone to the same secondary zone as the source instance. This value cannot be the same as the preferred_zone field. This field applies to all DB types.
---@field kind? string This is always `sql#cloneContext`.
---@field destinationProject? string Optional. The project ID of the destination project where the cloned instance will be created. To perform a cross-project clone, this field is required. If not specified, the clone is created in the same project as the source instance.
---@field destinationNetwork? string Optional. The fully qualified URI of the VPC network to which the cloned instance will be connected via private services access for private IP. For example:`projects/my-network-project/global/networks/my-network`. This field is only required for cross-project cloning.
---@field allocatedIpRange? string The name of the allocated ip range for the private ip Cloud SQL instance. For example: "google-managed-services-default". If set, the cloned instance ip will be created in the allocated range. The range name must comply with [RFC 1035](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc1035). Specifically, the name must be 1-63 characters long and match the regular expression [a-z]([-a-z0-9]*[a-z0-9])?. Reserved for future use.
---@field destinationInstanceName? string Required. Name of the Cloud SQL instance to be created as a clone.
---@field pointInTime? string Timestamp, if specified, identifies the time to which the source instance is cloned.
---@field preferredZone? string Optional. Copy clone and point-in-time recovery clone of an instance to the specified zone. If no zone is specified, clone to the same primary zone as the source instance. This field applies to all DB types.
---@field sourceInstanceDeletionTime? string The timestamp used to identify the time when the source instance is deleted. If this instance is deleted, then you must set the timestamp.
---@field binLogCoordinates? gcp.sqladmin_v1.BinLogCoordinates Binary log coordinates, if specified, identify the position up to which the source instance is cloned. If not specified, the source instance is cloned up to the most recent binary log coordinates.
---@field pitrTimestampMs? string Reserved for future use.
---@field databaseNames? gcp.sqladmin_v1.StringList (SQL Server only) Clone only the specified databases from the source instance. Clone all databases if empty.

---@class gcp.sqladmin_v1.CloneInstancesRequest
---@field cloneContext? gcp.sqladmin_v1.CloneContext Required. Contains details about the clone operation.
---@field project string Required. Project ID of the source Cloud SQL instance.
---@field location? string Optional. Region of the Cloud SQL instance.
---@field instance string Required. The ID of the Cloud SQL instance to be cloned (source). This does not include the project ID.

