---@alias gcp.sqladmin_v1.ConnectionPoolFlagsList gcp.sqladmin_v1.ConnectionPoolFlags[]

---@class gcp.sqladmin_v1.CreateBackupBackupsRequest
---@field type? gcp.sqladmin_v1.BackupTypeEnum|string Output only. The type of this backup. The type can be "AUTOMATED", "ON_DEMAND" or “FINAL”.
---@field location? string The storage location of the backups. The location can be multi-regional.
---@field maxChargeableBytes? string Output only. The maximum chargeable bytes for the backup.
---@field instanceSettings? gcp.sqladmin_v1.DatabaseInstance Optional. Output only. The instance setting of the source instance that's associated with this backup.
---@field name? string Output only. The resource name of the backup. Format: projects/{project}/backups/{backup}.
---@field kmsKeyVersion? string Output only. This output contains the encryption status for a backup and the version of the KMS key that's used to encrypt the Cloud SQL instance.
---@field selfLink? string Output only. The URI of this resource.
---@field databaseVersion? gcp.sqladmin_v1.BackupDatabaseVersionEnum|string Output only. The database version of the instance of at the time this backup was made.
---@field description? string The description of this backup.
---@field kind? string Output only. This is always `sql#backup`.
---@field ttlDays? string Input only. The time-to-live (TTL) interval for this resource (in days). For example: ttlDays:7, means 7 days from the current time. The expiration time can't exceed 365 days from the time that the backup is created.
---@field error? gcp.sqladmin_v1.OperationError Output only. Information about why the backup operation fails (for example, when the backup state fails).
---@field instanceDeletionTime? string Optional. Output only. Timestamp in UTC of when the instance associated with this backup is deleted.
---@field satisfiesPzi? boolean Output only. This status indicates whether the backup satisfies PZI. The status is reserved for future use.
---@field kmsKey? string Output only. This output contains the encryption configuration for a backup and the resource name of the KMS key for disk encryption.
---@field backupInterval? gcp.sqladmin_v1.Interval Output only. This output contains the following values: start_time: All database writes up to this time are available. end_time: Any database writes after this time aren't available.
---@field timeZone? string Output only. This output contains a backup time zone. If a Cloud SQL for SQL Server instance has a different time zone from the backup's time zone, then the restore to the instance doesn't happen.
---@field instance? string The name of the source database instance.
---@field state? gcp.sqladmin_v1.BackupStateEnum|string Output only. The status of this backup.
---@field backupKind? gcp.sqladmin_v1.BackupBackupKindEnum|string Output only. Specifies the kind of backup, PHYSICAL or DEFAULT_SNAPSHOT.
---@field satisfiesPzs? boolean Output only. This status indicates whether the backup satisfies PZS. The status is reserved for future use.
---@field expiryTime? string Backup expiration time. A UTC timestamp of when this backup expired.
---@field backupRun? string Output only. The mapping to backup run resource used for IAM validations.
---@field parent string Required. The parent resource where this backup is created. Format: projects/{project}

---@class gcp.sqladmin_v1.CreateBlueGreenDeploymentsRequest
---@field description? string Optional. User-provided description for the deployment. The description can be up to 255 characters long.
---@field requestedConfig? gcp.sqladmin_v1.RequestedConfig Optional. Immutable. Optional on create, and immutable. The configuration intended for the target instance(s) when the deployment was created.
---@field errorDetail? string Output only. Provides details on why switchover is not possible. This field is empty unless a switchover attempt failed or the state is `SWITCHOVER_NOT_READY`. Example: "The target database version does not match the source instance database version."
---@field switchoverTargetInstance? string Output only. The full resource name of the primary target instance (the "green" instance) that will be promoted during switchover. This field is always populated once the deployment is created. Format: projects/{project}/instances/{instance}
---@field sourceInstance? string Required. Immutable. Required on create, and immutable. The full resource name of the source instance (the "blue" instance). Format: projects/{project}/instances/{instance}
---@field deploymentTasks? gcp.sqladmin_v1.DeploymentTasks Output only. Combined list of tasks for all paired nodes.
---@field name? string Output only. Identifier. The full resource name of the deployment. Format: projects/{project}/locations/{location}/blueGreenDeployments/{deployment_id}
---@field createTime? string Output only. The time when the deployment was created. Example: `2024-01-01T00:00:00Z`
---@field deploymentMappings? gcp.sqladmin_v1.SourceTargetPairedNodeList Output only. A list representing the pairs of source and target instances in the deployment.
---@field state? gcp.sqladmin_v1.BlueGreenDeploymentStateEnum|string Output only. The current state of the blue-green deployment.
---@field parent string Required. The parent resource where this blue-green deployment will be created. Format: projects/{project}/locations/{location}
---@field blueGreenDeploymentId? string Required. The ID to use for the blue-green deployment, which will become the final component of the deployment's resource name. The ID must be unique within the given project and location and between 2-63 characters.

---@class gcp.sqladmin_v1.CreateEphemeralSslCertsRequest
---@field access_token? string Access token to include in the signed certificate.
---@field public_key? string PEM encoded public key to include in the signed certificate.
---@field location? string Optional. Region of the Cloud SQL instance.
---@field project string Project ID of the Cloud SQL project.
---@field instance string Cloud SQL instance ID. This does not include the project ID.

---Data cache configurations.
---@class gcp.sqladmin_v1.DataCacheConfig
---@field dataCacheEnabled? boolean Whether data cache is enabled for the instance.

---Represents a SQL database on the Cloud SQL instance.
