---@field name? string The name of the flag. These flags are passed at instance startup, so include both server options and system variables. Flags are specified with underscores, not hyphens. For more information, see [Configuring Database Flags](https://cloud.google.com/sql/docs/mysql/flags) in the Cloud SQL documentation.

---@alias gcp.sqladmin_v1.DatabaseFlagsList gcp.sqladmin_v1.DatabaseFlags[]

---A Cloud SQL instance resource.
---@class gcp.sqladmin_v1.DatabaseInstance
---@field suspensionReason? gcp.sqladmin_v1.DatabaseInstanceSuspensionReasonItemEnumList If the instance state is SUSPENDED, the reason for the suspension.
---@field onPremisesConfiguration? gcp.sqladmin_v1.OnPremisesConfiguration Configuration specific to on-premises instances.
---@field scheduledMaintenance? gcp.sqladmin_v1.SqlScheduledMaintenance The start time of any upcoming scheduled maintenance for this instance.
---@field satisfiesPzs? boolean This status indicates whether the instance satisfies PZS. The status is reserved for future use.
---@field settings? gcp.sqladmin_v1.Settings The user settings.
---@field switchTransactionLogsToCloudStorageEnabled? boolean Input only. Whether Cloud SQL is enabled to switch storing point-in-time recovery log files from a data disk to Cloud Storage.
---@field writeEndpoint? string Output only. The dns name of the primary instance in a replication group.
---@field connectionName? string Connection name of the Cloud SQL instance used in connection strings.
---@field databaseCenterIntegration? gcp.sqladmin_v1.DatabaseInstanceDatabaseCenterIntegrationEnum|string Optional. State of the Database Center integration for this instance. When unspecified, Database Center integration is enabled by default.
---@field primaryDnsName? string Output only. DEPRECATED: please use write_endpoint instead.
---@field replicaConfiguration? gcp.sqladmin_v1.ReplicaConfiguration Configuration specific to failover replicas and read replicas.
---@field selfLink? string The URI of this resource.
---@field availableMaintenanceVersions? gcp.sqladmin_v1.StringList Output only. List all maintenance versions applicable on the instance
---@field pscServiceAttachmentLink? string Output only. The link to service attachment of PSC instance.
---@field databaseInstalledVersion? string Output only. Stores the current database version running on the instance including minor version such as `MYSQL_8_0_18`.
---@field geminiConfig? gcp.sqladmin_v1.GeminiInstanceConfig Gemini instance configuration.
---@field backendType? gcp.sqladmin_v1.DatabaseInstanceBackendTypeEnum|string The backend type. `SECOND_GEN`: Cloud SQL database instance. `EXTERNAL`: A database server that is not managed by Google. This property is read-only; use the `tier` property in the `settings` object to determine the database type.
---@field ipAddresses? gcp.sqladmin_v1.IpMappingList The assigned IP addresses for the instance.
---@field dnsName? string Output only. The dns name of the instance.
---@field instanceType? gcp.sqladmin_v1.DatabaseInstanceInstanceTypeEnum|string The instance type.
---@field diskEncryptionConfiguration? gcp.sqladmin_v1.DiskEncryptionConfiguration Disk encryption configuration specific to an instance.
---@field serviceAccountEmailAddress? string The service account email address assigned to the instance.\This property is read-only.
---@field secondaryGceZone? string The Compute Engine zone that the failover instance is currently serving from for a regional instance. This value could be different from the zone that was specified when the instance was created if the instance has failed over to its secondary/failover zone.
---@field dnsNames? gcp.sqladmin_v1.DnsNameMappingList Output only. The list of DNS names used by this instance.
---@field project? string The project ID of the project containing the Cloud SQL instance. The Google apps domain is prefixed if applicable.
---@field etag? string This field is deprecated and will be removed from a future version of the API. Use the `settings.settingsVersion` field instead.
---@field tags? gcp.sqladmin_v1.StringMap Optional. Input only. Immutable. Tag keys and tag values that are bound to this instance. You must represent each item in the map as: `"" : ""`. For example, a single resource can have the following tags: ``` "123/environment": "production", "123/costCenter": "marketing", ``` For more information on tag creation and management, see https://cloud.google.com/resource-manager/docs/tags/tags-overview.
---@field maxDiskSize? string The maximum disk size of the instance in bytes.
---@field ipv6Address? string The IPv6 address assigned to the instance. (Deprecated) This property was applicable only to First Generation instances.
---@field replicationCluster? gcp.sqladmin_v1.ReplicationCluster Optional. A primary instance and disaster recovery (DR) replica pair. A DR replica is a cross-region replica that you designate for failover in the event that the primary instance experiences regional failure. Applicable to MySQL and PostgreSQL.
---@field maintenanceVersion? string The current software version on the instance.
---@field includeReplicasForMajorVersionUpgrade? boolean Input only. Determines whether an in-place major version upgrade of replicas happens when an in-place major version upgrade of a primary instance is initiated.
---@field satisfiesPzi? boolean Output only. This status indicates whether the instance satisfies PZI. The status is reserved for future use.
---@field gceZone? string The Compute Engine zone that the instance is currently serving from. This value could be different from the zone that was specified when the instance was created if the instance has failed over to its secondary zone. WARNING: Changing this might restart the instance.
---@field skipPrecheck? boolean Optional. Input only. Determines whether the precheck step is skipped during a major version upgrade.
---@field outOfDiskReport? gcp.sqladmin_v1.SqlOutOfDiskReport This field represents the report generated by the proactive database wellness job for OutOfDisk issues. * Writers: * the proactive database wellness job for OOD. * Readers: * the proactive database wellness job
---@field replicaNames? gcp.sqladmin_v1.StringList The replicas of the instance.
---@field failoverReplica? gcp.sqladmin_v1.DatabaseInstanceFailoverReplica The name and status of the failover replica.
---@field deploymentInfo? gcp.sqladmin_v1.BlueGreenDeploymentInfo Output only. Deployment info for the instance. This is set if the instance is currently part of any blue-green setup.
---@field serverCaCert? gcp.sqladmin_v1.SslCert SSL configuration.
---@field region? string The geographical region of the Cloud SQL instance. It can be one of the [regions](https://cloud.google.com/sql/docs/mysql/locations#location-r) where Cloud SQL operates: For example, `asia-east1`, `europe-west1`, and `us-central1`. The default value is `us-central1`.
---@field nodes? gcp.sqladmin_v1.PoolNodeConfigList Output only. Entries containing information about each read pool node of the read pool.
---@field upgradableDatabaseVersions? gcp.sqladmin_v1.AvailableDatabaseVersionList Output only. All database versions that are available for upgrade.
---@field state? gcp.sqladmin_v1.DatabaseInstanceStateEnum|string The current serving state of the Cloud SQL instance.
---@field diskEncryptionStatus? gcp.sqladmin_v1.DiskEncryptionStatus Disk encryption status specific to an instance.
---@field databaseCenterIntegrationEnabled? boolean Optional. If true, instance metadata is sent to the Database Center. If false, instance metadata is not sent to the Database Center.
---@field masterInstanceName? string The name of the instance which will act as primary in the replication setup.
---@field databaseVersion? gcp.sqladmin_v1.DatabaseInstanceDatabaseVersionEnum|string The database engine type and version. The `databaseVersion` field cannot be changed after instance creation.
---@field createTime? string Output only. The time when the instance was created in [RFC 3339](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc3339) format, for example `2012-11-15T16:19:00.094Z`.
---@field sqlNetworkArchitecture? gcp.sqladmin_v1.DatabaseInstanceSqlNetworkArchitectureEnum|string
---@field nodeCount? number The number of read pool nodes in a read pool.
---@field name? string Name of the Cloud SQL instance. This does not include the project ID.
---@field currentDiskSize? string The current disk usage of the instance in bytes. This property has been deprecated. Use the "cloudsql.googleapis.com/database/disk/bytes_used" metric in Cloud Monitoring API instead. Please see [this announcement](https://groups.google.com/d/msg/google-cloud-sql-announce/I_7-F9EBhT0/BtvFtdFeAgAJ) for details.
---@field kind? string This is always `sql#instance`.
---@field rootPassword? string Initial root password. Use only on creation. You must set root passwords before you can connect to PostgreSQL instances.

