---Database instance import context.
---@class gcp.sqladmin_v1.ImportContext
---@field tdeImportOptions? gcp.sqladmin_v1.ImportContextTdeImportOptions Optional. Import parameters specific to SQL Server TDE certificates
---@field database? string The target database for the import. If `fileType` is `SQL`, this field is required only if the import file does not specify a database, and is overridden by any database specification in the import file. For entire instance parallel import operations, the database is overridden by the database name stored in subdirectory name. If `fileType` is `CSV`, one database must be specified.
---@field sqlImportOptions? gcp.sqladmin_v1.ImportContextSqlImportOptions Optional. Options for importing data from SQL statements.
---@field csvImportOptions? gcp.sqladmin_v1.ImportContextCsvImportOptions Options for importing data as CSV.
---@field importUser? string The PostgreSQL user for this import operation. PostgreSQL instances only.
---@field uri? string Path to the import file in Cloud Storage, in the form `gs://bucketName/fileName`. Compressed gzip files (.gz) are supported when `fileType` is `SQL`. The instance must have write permissions to the bucket and read access to the file.
---@field fileType? gcp.sqladmin_v1.ImportContextFileTypeEnum|string The file type for the specified uri.\`SQL`: The file contains SQL statements. \`CSV`: The file contains CSV data.
---@field kind? string This is always `sql#importContext`.
---@field bakImportOptions? gcp.sqladmin_v1.ImportContextBakImportOptions Import parameters specific to SQL Server .BAK files

---@class gcp.sqladmin_v1.ImportContextBakImportOptions
---@field encryptionOptions? gcp.sqladmin_v1.ImportContextBakImportOptionsEncryptionOptions
---@field striped? boolean Whether or not the backup set being restored is striped. Applies only to Cloud SQL for SQL Server.
---@field noRecovery? boolean Whether or not the backup importing will restore database with NORECOVERY option. Applies only to Cloud SQL for SQL Server.
---@field stopAtMark? string Optional. The marked transaction where the import should stop. This field is equivalent to the STOPATMARK keyword and applies to Cloud SQL for SQL Server only.
---@field bakType? gcp.sqladmin_v1.ImportContextBakImportOptionsBakTypeEnum|string Type of the bak content, FULL or DIFF
---@field recoveryOnly? boolean Whether or not the backup importing request will just bring database online without downloading Bak content only one of "no_recovery" and "recovery_only" can be true otherwise error will return. Applies only to Cloud SQL for SQL Server.
---@field stopAt? string Optional. The timestamp when the import should stop. This timestamp is in the [RFC 3339](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc3339) format (for example, `2023-10-01T16:19:00.094`). This field is equivalent to the STOPAT keyword and applies to Cloud SQL for SQL Server only.

---@alias gcp.sqladmin_v1.ImportContextBakImportOptionsBakTypeEnum "BAK_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"FULL"|"DIFF"|"TLOG"

---@class gcp.sqladmin_v1.ImportContextBakImportOptionsEncryptionOptions
---@field keepEncrypted? boolean Optional. Whether the imported file remains encrypted.
---@field certPath? string Path to the Certificate (.cer) in Cloud Storage, in the form `gs://bucketName/fileName`. The instance must have write permissions to the bucket and read access to the file.
---@field pvkPath? string Path to the Certificate Private Key (.pvk) in Cloud Storage, in the form `gs://bucketName/fileName`. The instance must have write permissions to the bucket and read access to the file.
---@field pvkPassword? string Password that encrypts the private key

---@class gcp.sqladmin_v1.ImportContextCsvImportOptions
---@field table? string The table to which CSV data is imported.
---@field quoteCharacter? string Specifies the quoting character to be used when a data value is quoted.
---@field escapeCharacter? string Specifies the character that should appear before a data character that needs to be escaped.
---@field linesTerminatedBy? string This is used to separate lines. If a line does not contain all fields, the rest of the columns are set to their default values.
---@field columns? gcp.sqladmin_v1.StringList The columns to which CSV data is imported. If not specified, all columns of the database table are loaded with CSV data.
