---Database instance restore from backup context. Backup context contains source instance id and project id.
---@class gcp.sqladmin_v1.RestoreBackupContext
---@field instanceId? string The ID of the instance that the backup was taken from.
---@field kind? string This is always `sql#restoreBackupContext`.
---@field backupRunId? string The ID of the backup run to restore from.
---@field project? string The full project ID of the source instance.

---@class gcp.sqladmin_v1.RestoreBackupInstancesRequest
---@field restoreInstanceSettings? gcp.sqladmin_v1.DatabaseInstance Optional. By using this parameter, Cloud SQL overrides any instance settings stored in the backup you are restoring from. You can't change the instance's major database version and you can only increase the disk size. You can use this field to restore new instances only. This field is not applicable for restore to existing instances.
---@field backup? string The name of the backup that's used to restore a Cloud SQL instance: Format: projects/{project-id}/backups/{backup-uid}. Only one of restore_backup_context, backup, backupdr_backup can be passed to the input.
---@field ignoreMaintenanceVersion? boolean Optional. If true, the restore operation proceeds even if the target instance's maintenance version is older than the source instance's maintenance version.
---@field restoreInstanceClearOverridesFieldNames? gcp.sqladmin_v1.StringList Optional. This field has the same purpose as restore_instance_settings, changes any instance settings stored in the backup you are restoring from. With the difference that these fields are cleared in the settings.
---@field backupdrBackup? string The name of the backup that's used to restore a Cloud SQL instance: Format: "projects/{project-id}/locations/{location}/backupVaults/{backupvault}/dataSources/{datasource}/backups/{backup-uid}". Only one of restore_backup_context, backup, backupdr_backup can be passed to the input.
---@field restoreBackupContext? gcp.sqladmin_v1.RestoreBackupContext Parameters required to perform the restore backup operation.
---@field location? string Optional. Region of the Cloud SQL instance.
---@field project string Project ID of the project that contains the instance.
---@field instance string Cloud SQL instance ID. This does not include the project ID.

