---Database instance settings.
---@class gcp.sqladmin_v1.Settings
---@field entraidConfig? gcp.sqladmin_v1.SqlServerEntraIdConfig Optional. The Microsoft Entra ID configuration for the SQL Server instance.
---@field dataCacheConfig? gcp.sqladmin_v1.DataCacheConfig Configuration for data cache.
---@field autoUpgradeEnabled? boolean Optional. Cloud SQL for MySQL auto-upgrade configuration. When this parameter is set to true, auto-upgrade is enabled for MySQL 8.0 minor versions. The MySQL version must be 8.0.35 or higher.
---@field backupConfiguration? gcp.sqladmin_v1.BackupConfiguration The daily backup configuration for the instance.
---@field userLabels? gcp.sqladmin_v1.StringMap User-provided labels, represented as a dictionary where each label is a single key value pair.
---@field connectionPoolConfig? gcp.sqladmin_v1.ConnectionPoolConfig Optional. The managed connection pooling configuration for the instance.
---@field advancedMachineFeatures? gcp.sqladmin_v1.AdvancedMachineFeatures Specifies advanced machine configuration for the instances relevant only for SQL Server.
---@field ipConfiguration? gcp.sqladmin_v1.IpConfiguration The settings for IP Management. This allows to enable or disable the instance IP and manage which external networks can connect to the instance. The IPv4 address cannot be disabled for Second Generation instances.
---@field databaseFlags? gcp.sqladmin_v1.DatabaseFlagsList The database flags passed to the instance at startup.
---@field crashSafeReplicationEnabled? boolean Configuration specific to read replica instances. Indicates whether database flags for crash-safe replication are enabled. This property was only applicable to First Generation instances.
---@field readPoolAutoScaleConfig? gcp.sqladmin_v1.ReadPoolAutoScaleConfig Optional. The read pool auto-scale configuration for the instance.
---@field performanceCaptureConfig? gcp.sqladmin_v1.PerformanceCaptureConfig Optional. Configuration for Performance Capture, provides diagnostic metrics during high load situations.
---@field settingsVersion? string The version of instance settings. This is a required field for update method to make sure concurrent updates are handled properly. During update, use the most recent settingsVersion value for this instance and do not try to update this value.
---@field finalBackupConfig? gcp.sqladmin_v1.FinalBackupConfig Optional. The final backup configuration for the instance.
---@field kind? string This is always `sql#settings`.
---@field connectorEnforcement? gcp.sqladmin_v1.SettingsConnectorEnforcementEnum|string Specifies if connections must use Cloud SQL connectors. Option values include the following: `NOT_REQUIRED` (Cloud SQL instances can be connected without Cloud SQL Connectors) and `REQUIRED` (Only allow connections that use Cloud SQL Connectors). Note that using REQUIRED disables all existing authorized networks. If this field is not specified when creating a new instance, NOT_REQUIRED is used. If this field is not specified when patching or updating an existing instance, it is left unchanged in the instance.
---@field collation? string The name of server Instance collation.
---@field enableGoogleMlIntegration? boolean Optional. When this parameter is set to true, Cloud SQL instances can connect to Vertex AI to pass requests for real-time predictions and insights to the AI. The default value is false. This applies only to Cloud SQL for MySQL and Cloud SQL for PostgreSQL instances.
---@field denyMaintenancePeriods? gcp.sqladmin_v1.DenyMaintenancePeriodList Deny maintenance periods
---@field retainBackupsOnDelete? boolean Optional. When this parameter is set to true, Cloud SQL retains backups of the instance even after the instance is deleted. The ON_DEMAND backup will be retained until customer deletes the backup or the project. The AUTOMATED backup will be retained based on the backups retention setting.
---@field replicationType? gcp.sqladmin_v1.SettingsReplicationTypeEnum|string The type of replication this instance uses. This can be either `ASYNCHRONOUS` or `SYNCHRONOUS`. (Deprecated) This property was only applicable to First Generation instances.
---@field storageAutoResizeLimit? string The maximum size to which storage capacity can be automatically increased. The default value is 0, which specifies that there is no limit.
---@field pricingPlan? gcp.sqladmin_v1.SettingsPricingPlanEnum|string The pricing plan for this instance. This can be either `PER_USE` or `PACKAGE`. Only `PER_USE` is supported for Second Generation instances.
---@field passwordValidationPolicy? gcp.sqladmin_v1.PasswordValidationPolicy The local user password validation policy of the instance for PostgreSQL and MySQL.
---@field dataApiAccess? gcp.sqladmin_v1.SettingsDataApiAccessEnum|string This parameter controls whether to allow using ExecuteSql API to connect to the instance. Not allowed by default.
---@field activeDirectoryConfig? gcp.sqladmin_v1.SqlActiveDirectoryConfig Active Directory configuration, relevant only for Cloud SQL for SQL Server.
---@field maintenanceWindow? gcp.sqladmin_v1.MaintenanceWindow The maintenance window for this instance. This specifies when the instance can be restarted for maintenance purposes.
---@field tier? string The tier (or machine type) for this instance, for example `db-custom-1-3840`. WARNING: Changing this restarts the instance.
---@field edition? gcp.sqladmin_v1.SettingsEditionEnum|string Optional. The edition type of the Cloud SQL instance.
---@field dataDiskProvisionedIops? string Optional. Provisioned number of I/O operations per second for the data disk. This field is only used for hyperdisk-balanced disk types.
---@field dataDiskProvisionedThroughput? string Optional. Provisioned throughput measured in MiB per second for the data disk. This field is only used for hyperdisk-balanced disk types.
---@field authorizedGaeApplications? gcp.sqladmin_v1.StringList The App Engine app IDs that can access this instance. (Deprecated) Applied to First Generation instances only.
---@field dataDiskSizeGb? string The size of data disk, in GB. The data disk size minimum is 10GB.
---@field replicationLagMaxSeconds? number Optional. Configuration value for recreation of replica after certain replication lag
---@field sqlServerAuditConfig? gcp.sqladmin_v1.SqlServerAuditConfig SQL Server specific audit configuration.
---@field enableDataplexIntegration? boolean Optional. By default, Cloud SQL instances have schema extraction disabled for Dataplex. When this parameter is set to true, schema extraction for Dataplex on Cloud SQL instances is activated.
---@field acceleratedReplicaMode? boolean Optional. Whether the replica is in accelerated mode. This feature is in private preview and requires allowlisting to take effect.
---@field activationPolicy? gcp.sqladmin_v1.SettingsActivationPolicyEnum|string The activation policy specifies when the instance is activated; it is applicable only when the instance state is RUNNABLE. Valid values: * `ALWAYS`: The instance is on, and remains so even in the absence of connection requests. * `NEVER`: The instance is off; it is not activated, even if a connection request arrives.
---@field timeZone? string Server timezone, relevant only for Cloud SQL for SQL Server.
---@field deletionProtectionEnabled? boolean Configuration to protect against accidental instance deletion.
---@field databaseReplicationEnabled? boolean Configuration specific to read replica instances. Indicates whether replication is enabled or not. WARNING: Changing this restarts the instance.
---@field storageAutoResize? boolean Configuration to increase storage size automatically. The default value is true.
---@field dataDiskType? gcp.sqladmin_v1.SettingsDataDiskTypeEnum|string The type of data disk: `PD_SSD` (default) or `PD_HDD`. Not used for First Generation instances.
---@field insightsConfig? gcp.sqladmin_v1.InsightsConfig Insights configuration, for now relevant only for Postgres.
---@field availabilityType? gcp.sqladmin_v1.SettingsAvailabilityTypeEnum|string Availability type. Potential values: * `ZONAL`: The instance serves data from only one zone. Outages in that zone affect data accessibility. * `REGIONAL`: The instance can serve data from more than one zone in a region (it is highly available)./ For more information, see [Overview of the High Availability Configuration](https://cloud.google.com/sql/docs/mysql/high-availability).
---@field locationPreference? gcp.sqladmin_v1.LocationPreference The location preference settings. This allows the instance to be located as near as possible to either an App Engine app or Compute Engine zone for better performance. App Engine co-location was only applicable to First Generation instances.
