---The context for the `StartWorkloadCapture` operation, which contains details to start recording the workload (SQL queries) on a Cloud SQL instance.
---@class gcp.sqladmin_v1.StartWorkloadCaptureContext
---@field replayInstance? string Optional. Required if `enable_live_replay` is true. The name of the Cloud SQL instance where the captured workload (SQL queries) is being executed, excluding the project ID (for example, `my-replay-instance`). The instance name must start with a lowercase letter and contain only lowercase letters, numbers, and hyphens. The combined length of `project-ID:instance-name` must be 98 characters or less.
---@field enableLiveReplay? boolean Optional. If true, the captured workload is simultaneously executed on a separate, ephemeral Cloud SQL instance. This "live replay" instance is automatically provisioned and is cloned from the source instance. If false (the default), the workload is only stored and no live replay occurs. It can be replayed later using a separate `StartWorkloadReplayRequest`. Note: The workload capture runs continuously until an explicit `StopWorkloadCaptureRequest` is issued.

---@class gcp.sqladmin_v1.StartWorkloadCapturesRequest
---@field startWorkloadCaptureContext? gcp.sqladmin_v1.StartWorkloadCaptureContext Optional. Contains details about the start workload capture operation.
---@field instance string Required. Cloud SQL instance ID. This does not include the project ID.
---@field project string Required. Project ID of the project that contains the instance.

---The context for the `StartWorkloadReplay` operation, which contains details about starting the execution of a captured workload (recorded read and write SQL queries) on a replay instance (the Cloud SQL instance where the recorded SQL queries are executed).
---@class gcp.sqladmin_v1.StartWorkloadReplayContext
---@field workloadId? string Output only. The ID of the workload to start executing on the replay instance. Each workload capture generates a unique ID in the format `workload-` (for example, `workload-1786046400`). Use this ID to start executing the recorded SQL queries.
---@field replayInstance? string Required. The name of the Cloud SQL instance where the captured workload (SQL queries) is being executed, excluding the project ID (for example, `my-replay-instance`). The instance name must start with a lowercase letter and contain only lowercase letters, numbers, and hyphens. The combined length of `project-ID:instance-name` must be 98 characters or less.

---The `Status` type defines a logical error model that is suitable for different programming environments, including REST APIs and RPC APIs. It is used by [gRPC](https://github.com/grpc). Each `Status` message contains three pieces of data: error code, error message, and error details. You can find out more about this error model and how to work with it in the [API Design Guide](https://cloud.google.com/apis/design/errors).
---@class gcp.sqladmin_v1.Status
---@field code? number The status code, which should be an enum value of google.rpc.Code.
---@field message? string A developer-facing error message, which should be in English. Any user-facing error message should be localized and sent in the google.rpc.Status.details field, or localized by the client.
---@field details? gcp.sqladmin_v1.DocumentMapList A list of messages that carry the error details. There is a common set of message types for APIs to use.

---@class gcp.sqladmin_v1.StopReplayWorkloadCapturesRequest
